ryline changes with every episode  but you'll also find super sarcastic  characters and running gags that will  make you laugh out loud the loud house  features scenes and moments that will  definitely go over kids heads which  means the show is perfect for adults too  whether you've grown up in a big family  or are an only child this show will make  you fill all types of ways about the  life as you can see the two storylines  are entirely different but they're also  based on the same relatable characters  just like Spongebob the loud house  constantly raises questions that defy  cartoon logic overall both shows feature  wacky moments both shows have hilarious  characters and both shows attract a  crowd of a broad demographic now let's  check both of these out in more detail  main characters so let's talk about the  main characters of both shows starting  with SpongeBob SquarePants SpongeBob has  a strange variety of main characters  that all include underwater creatures  that were given a certain personality  that's not really stereotypical to their  nature we see spongebob they have to go  lucky sponge that doesn't seem to be  bothered by anything in life then we  have the dim-witted Patrick who's well  living under a rock quite literally  another is the money hungry mr. Krabs  the owner of Krusty Krabs where Sponge  Bob works Squidward is SpongeBob's a  grumpy neighbor who just can't seem to  understand why these annoying creatures  just can't leave him alone we also  frequently see plankton who desperately  tries to do whatever he can to steal the  secret krabby patty formula to make his  own restaurant  what makes spongebob characters so  amazing is that their characters are  incredibly surprising they don't fit  into any kind of real stereotypes and  even Patrick and sometimes surprise you  in saying something completely genius  Squidward who seems to be grumpy most of  the time also has almost 500  self-portraits in his home for whatever  reason the characters have complex  personalities that actually work well  and allow for plenty of storylines and  surprising discoveries but on the other  side we have the loud house where its  main characters are obviously based on  some of the biggest stereotypes each of  the sisters has a strong personality  that can sometimes be seen quite  stereotypical for example Laurie is the  grumpy oldest sister Luna is a rock  chick Lucy is the moody poetry girl Lola  is a pageant princess Lynn is sporty and  competitive while that's pretty cool to  see it does sometimes limit the  storylines and make the fans questioned  why a character stepped out of their  stereotype since it's often highlighted  so much it's very clear that these type  of characters can definitely be found in  every family or perhaps in every life  phase which makes this show that much  more interesting to watch this  allows us to easily follow the story and  we think we automatically know what to  expect from a character in the story  which sometimes adds an element of  surprise while there are definitely  things the loud house could work on when  it comes to their characters we have to  admit that they're definitely more  relatable than Sponge Bob side  characters as we all know spongebob is  full of side characters that definitely  make the show better than it would have  been otherwise we're introduced to  amazing characters like squilliam who's  the only one that can make Squidward  blush or you know show any kind of  positive emotion there's pearl Krabs  who's mr. Krabs daughter who no one  seems to question the fact that she's a  whale but one can only assume how that  happened people also love mrs. puff the  driving instructor who definitely  doesn't have enough nerves to endure  spongebob and she probably represents a  lot of teachers out there and then  there's of course Mermaid Man and  Barnacle Boy the ocean superheroes  spongebob side characters are absolutely  hilarious and they really are the ones  that m