 to watch this show  when they were kids because Sponge Bob  has been around since 1999 it means a  lot of the viewers grew up with the show  and are now adults who fondly remember  early seasons in 2011 Sponge Bob  Saturday morning premiere drew in five  million viewers and in 2013 a  competitive rating of 1.1 was noted  between the demographic of 18 to 49  years of age that's pretty impressive  for a show like spongebob and there's  definitely a reason why it remains so  popular the demographic seems to have  changed over the years and now the show  can pull in a pretty decent age number  ranging from 2 to 14 in 2012 spongebob  even became one of the biggest shows in  Egypt where the show's merchandise  became an instant hit with street  vendors and even japan got on board with  this wacky show the loud houses story is  a little bit different surprisingly the  loud house pulled even larger numbers on  its debut premiere bringing in a total  of 2.28 viewers it's ranked high among  the critics and during the first year it  officially beats SpongeBob SquarePants  in ratings its viewers have remained  steady at almost 2 million per episode  and its debut officially stole  SpongeBob's mane age demographic which  is the ages from 2 to 11 the loud house  also has an impressive score of 80  percent on Rotten Tomatoes while the  score for SpongeBob SquarePants is 71  percent the canvas 2016 family cartoon  really go up against the old school show  such as spongebob in the long run well  we'll have to wait and see but so far it  seems like people just can't wait for  new seasons and new adventures of the  loud house of course the show still has  a long way to go but we feel like it's  definitely on the right track to take  SpongeBob's Nickelodeon crown what do  you think who would you pick as your  ultimate favorite cartoon we have to say  that both shows bring different elements  that make them completely unique and  it's almost impossible to choose the  winner of this crazy showdown  share your opinions in the comments  below and that's all for our video  thanks for watching and don't forget to  subscribe to the things see you next  time  [Music]

